<item>
            <title>[PARQUET-186] Poor performance in SnappyCodec because of string concat in tight loop</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-186</link>
                <project id="12315521" key="PARQUET">Parquet</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;String concatenation for SnappyUtil.validateBuffer which is called in a tight &lt;br/&gt;
loop from both compress/decompress.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This shows up as taking 60% of time in the profiler &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;  &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;static&lt;/span&gt; void validateBuffer(&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;byte&lt;/span&gt;[] buffer, &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; off, &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; len) {
    Preconditions.checkNotNull(buffer, &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;buffer&quot;&lt;/span&gt;);
    Preconditions.checkArgument(off &amp;gt;= 0 &amp;amp;&amp;amp; len &amp;gt;= 0 &amp;amp;&amp;amp; off &amp;lt;= buffer.length - len,
        &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;Invalid offset or length. Out of buffer bounds. buffer.length=&quot;&lt;/span&gt; + buffer.length
        + &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot; off=&quot;&lt;/span&gt; + off + &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot; len=&quot;&lt;/span&gt; + len);
  }
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="12774662">PARQUET-186</key>
            <summary>Poor performance in SnappyCodec because of string concat in tight loop</summary>
